<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<inkscape-extension xmlns="http://www.inkscape.org/namespace/inkscape/extension">
<name>NextDraw Naming</name>
<id>command.bantamtools.nextdraw_naming</id>
<dependency type="extension">org.inkscape.output.svg.inkscape</dependency>
<dependency type="executable" location="extensions">nextdraw_naming.py</dependency>



<param name="mode" type="notebook" >
<page name="list_names" gui-text="Read NextDraw Name">

<label appearance="header">
Read NextDraw Nickname
</label>

<label indent="2"  xml:space="preserve">
Click "Apply" to read and list all NextDraw units found via
USB. Each is listed by assigned USB Nickname (if any) or by
USB port enumeration.
</label>

</page>


<page name="write_name" gui-text="Write NextDraw Name">

<label appearance="header">
Write NextDraw Nickname
</label>

<param indent="1" name="nickname" type="string" max_length="16" gui-text="Nickname:">East</param>

<label indent="2" xml:space="preserve">
Click "Apply" to assign the USB Nickname above to the
machine connected via USB. After the name change, the machine
will reboot to its power-on state. (If more than machine is
connected, only the first one found will be named.)

Names must be 3-16 characters long.

USB Nicknames are semi-permanent; they can be changed
by this utility and may be erased by firmware updates.

USB Nicknames may not be visible until after resetting the
machine manually and/or disconnecting it from USB.
</label>

</page>



<page name="about" gui-text="About">

<label indent="2" xml:space="preserve">
This extension allows you to assign a "USB Nickname" (a digital
name tag) to a given NextDraw, or to read out that name. 

USB Nicknames are not required, but can be helpful if you have
more than one NextDraw connected: You can specify which
NextDraw to plot to when using NextDraw Control.

Please be aware that updating your firmware may remove any
existing USB Nickname; resetting the configuration to default.
</label>


</page>

</param>


<effect needs-live-preview="false">
<object-type>all</object-type>
<effects-menu>
    <submenu name="Bantam Tools Utilities"/>
</effects-menu>
</effect>

<script>
<command location="extensions" interpreter="python">nextdraw_naming.py</command>
</script>

</inkscape-extension>